WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.482
Hi, I'm Confetti!

00:00:02.482 --> 00:00:06.852
Limite 1B Violetto is a small maths model sold as high-throughput.

00:00:06.852 --> 00:00:08.442
Its config shows why.

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:13.789
Three of every four blocks only look back a thousand and twenty-four tokens.

00:00:13.789 --> 00:00:16.367
Only twelve of forty-eight keep a growing cache.

00:00:19.567 --> 00:00:23.738
Most parts read like a speedrun changelog, and none costs anything at inference.

00:00:24.158 --> 00:00:28.800
A second embedding table feeds sixteen blocks' value path straight from the token id.

00:00:29.220 --> 00:00:32.434
Two dense shortcuts, at the half-way block and the exit, reach

00:00:32.434 --> 00:00:33.603
back to earlier blocks.

00:00:34.023 --> 00:00:37.388
Norms have no learnable gain, and the attention scale is pinned

00:00:37.388 --> 00:00:38.612
at zero point one.

00:00:39.833 --> 00:00:43.795
A windowed block looks back only a thousand and twenty-four tokens, with

00:00:43.795 --> 00:00:46.107
short rotary positions on half its channels.

00:00:46.527 --> 00:00:50.889
Every fourth block is global: it sees everything, with no positional encoding,

00:00:50.889 --> 00:00:52.707
relying on the causal mask.

00:00:53.983 --> 00:00:55.888
What does one token cost in one block?

00:00:56.308 --> 00:00:58.492
Keys and values, for two KV heads.

00:00:58.492 --> 00:01:00.053
Ten query heads share them.

00:01:00.473 --> 00:01:03.745
Each head is a hundred and twenty-eight wide, two bytes a number.

00:01:04.165 --> 00:01:05.951
A thousand and twenty-four bytes.

00:01:05.951 --> 00:01:10.236
At a hundred and thirty-one thousand tokens, a global block holds a

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:13.450
hundred and thirty-four megabytes; a windowed one, about one.

00:01:14.633 --> 00:01:18.955
In all: one point six five gigabytes, not six point four four.

00:01:18.955 --> 00:01:22.917
An eighty gigabyte card fits forty-four long problems instead of eleven.

00:01:24.017 --> 00:01:28.504
High throughput here means concurrency: forty-four long problems where eleven would fit.

00:01:28.504 --> 00:01:31.495
A ceiling from the config, not a measurement.

00:01:32.733 --> 00:01:36.449
To recap: windowed blocks, a few global ones without positions, and

00:01:36.449 --> 00:01:37.800
a much smaller cache.

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:40.382
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:40.382 --> 00:01:41.000
I'm Confetti.

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:41.309
Bye!
